{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1134","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1134","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1134\",\"parent_revision\":\"45fa202991dee39868a283b83f32be550aa63a1e971beb4ac1645ccdf2e547f0\",\"root_revision\":\"45fa202991dee39868a283b83f32be550aa63a1e971beb4ac1645ccdf2e547f0\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-05-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\noperations.py line 1558-1559 sets `entry[\\\"groomed\\\"] = True` unconditionally, discarding the date string stored in `item.groomed`. The BacklogItem model (models.py:448) stores groomed as `str` (e.g. \\\"2026-03-28\\\"). The fix is one line: change `entry[\\\"groomed\\\"] = True` to `entry[\\\"groomed\\\"] = item.groomed`.\\n\\n**Why it matters**: The staleness policy (and drift-check.md) needs the groom date to compute `git log --after=\\\"{groom_date}\\\"`. Without it, staleness detection cannot determine which commits postdate the last groom.\\n\\n**Backward compatibility**: A truthy string passes all existing `if entry[\\\"groomed\\\"]` checks. No callers break.\\n\\n**Acceptance criteria**:\\n- [ ] `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#N\\\", summary=False)` returns `groomed: \\\"YYYY-MM-DD\\\"` for groomed items\\n- [ ] `backlog_list` returns the date string in the `groomed` field (not `True`)\\n- [ ] Items with `groomed: true` (legacy boolean) continue to work \u2014 coerce to sentinel value or preserve as-is\\n- [ ] All existing tests pass\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix: backlog_view coerces groomed date string to boolean true \u2014 expose raw date** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research: staleness policy RT-ICA session 2026-03-30\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-30\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-02)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Staleness detection is blocked until the groom date is available in API responses. The bug discards a string value the model already stores correctly, making it a trivial one-line fix with outsized downstream impact.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: staleness policy (`drift-check.md`) cannot compute `git log --after='{groom_date}'` without the date\\n- Bottleneck: every consumer that needs to know when an item was last groomed receives `True` instead of a usable date\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Enables staleness detection to determine which commits postdate the last groom\\n- Callers receive a machine-readable date string usable in date comparisons and `git log --after` queries\\n- No caller breakage: a truthy string satisfies all existing `if entry['groomed']` checks\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `backlog_view` or `backlog_list` returns a groomed item, the `groomed` field contains the date string stored in frontmatter (e.g. `'2026-03-28'`). Items that have never been groomed return no `groomed` field (or `False`). Legacy items where frontmatter stores `groomed: true` (boolean) continue to evaluate as truthy.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `_build_list_entry` (operations.py ~line 1557) sets `entry['groomed'] = item.groomed` instead of `entry['groomed'] = True`\\n- `_item_to_view_result` (parsing.py ~line 827) sets `groomed=item.groomed` (preserving the string) instead of `groomed=bool(item.groomed)` (which collapses date strings to `True`)\\n- `ViewItemResult.groomed` and `ViewItemResultCompact.groomed` fields (models.py lines 519, 562) accept `str | bool` to accommodate both date strings and legacy boolean values\\n- `BacklogItem.groomed` (models.py line 448) is already typed as `str` \u2014 no change needed there\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `backlog_view(selector='#N', summary=False)` returns `groomed: 'YYYY-MM-DD'` for a groomed item whose frontmatter contains `groomed: '2026-03-28'`\\n2. `backlog_list()` returns the date string (not `True`) in the `groomed` field for groomed items\\n3. An item with frontmatter `groomed: true` (legacy boolean) still evaluates as truthy in `if item['groomed']` checks\\n4. An item with no `groomed` field in frontmatter returns no `groomed` key (or `False`) from both endpoints\\n5. All existing tests in `test_backlog_core_operations.py` pass without modification\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py line 1556-1557 \u2014 `_build_list_entry` coercion site |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/parsing.py line 827 \u2014 `_item_to_view_result` coercion site |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py line 448 \u2014 `BacklogItem.groomed: str` (correct) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py lines 519, 562 \u2014 `ViewItemResult.groomed: bool` and `ViewItemResultCompact.groomed: bool` (need widening to `str \\\\| bool`) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py line 1327 \u2014 existing `_build_list_entry` test class (no groomed date test exists yet) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: staleness policy implementation (drift-check.md groom-date computation)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 two one-line fixes (operations.py:1557 and parsing.py:827) plus a type annotation widening in models.py. No schema migration needed; string is truthy so no caller breaks.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n**Code paths that read `entry[\\\"groomed\\\"]` or `result.groomed`:**\\n\\n- `operations.py` `_build_list_entry` (line 2235) \u2014 emits `groomed` key into the list-item dict consumed by `backlog_list` callers\\n- `parsing.py` `view_result_from_local_item` (line 1106) \u2014 emits `ViewItemResult.groomed` consumed by `backlog_view` callers\\n- `operations.py` `view_item` (line 2804) \u2014 restores `result.groomed = item.metadata.groomed` after GitHub enrichment\\n- `parsing.py` lines 334\u2013336 \u2014 legacy fallback: sets `groomed = \\\"true\\\"` (string, not bool) when `## Groomed` exists in body but no frontmatter field\\n- `models.py` `ListEntry.groomed: NotRequired[str]` (line 460) \u2014 TypedDict for list response; callers trusting this type get a string\\n- `models.py` `ViewItemResult.groomed: str` and `ViewItemResultCompact.groomed: str` (lines 1130, 1183) \u2014 response models; both already typed as `str`\\n\\n**Downstream callers that depend on the groomed value:**\\n\\n- `drift-check.md` staleness policy \u2014 uses `git log --after=\\\"{groom_date}\\\"` to find commits postdating last groom; receives `True` (unusable) instead of a date string (fatal for staleness detection)\\n- Any MCP client reading `entry[\\\"groomed\\\"]` from `backlog_list` response to drive staleness or age computations\\n- `backlog_view` summary mode \u2014 surfaces `groomed` field in compact routing manifest consumed by grooming agents\\n\\n**Current state (verified 2026-05-24):**\\n`operations.py` already uses `entry[\\\"groomed\\\"] = item.groomed` (not `True`) and `parsing.py` already uses `groomed=item.metadata.groomed`. The `ViewItemResult.groomed` field is already typed as `str`. The `bool(item.groomed)` coercion referenced in the original description does NOT appear in the current codebase. The remaining gap is a missing regression test confirming the date string propagates end-to-end through `_build_list_entry`.\\n\\n### Implementation Plan\\n\\n**Current state (verified 2026-05-24):** The one-line fix described in the original description has already been applied. `operations.py` uses `entry[\\\"groomed\\\"] = item.groomed` (not `True`) and `parsing.py` uses `groomed=item.metadata.groomed`. `ViewItemResult.groomed` is already typed as `str`. No production code changes are required.\\n\\n**Remaining work \u2014 regression tests only:**\\n\\n1. `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` \u2014 add a test to `TestBuildListEntryTypeTopicFields` (or a new class) that creates a `BacklogItem` with `groomed=\\\"2026-03-28\\\"` and asserts `_build_list_entry` returns `entry[\\\"groomed\\\"] == \\\"2026-03-28\\\"` (not `True`)\\n2. `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_parsing.py` \u2014 extend the existing `view_result_from_local_item` test class with a case asserting `result.groomed == \\\"2026-03-28\\\"` for an item whose frontmatter has `groomed: 2026-03-28`\\n\\n**Validation commands:**\\n\\n```\\nuv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py::TestBuildListEntryTypeTopicFields -v\\nuv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_parsing.py -k groomed -v\\n```\\n\",\"digest\":\"6d4deb6d10b12c5ccefd2e8c948c39af356da0cf2b5dca6ab9c41f30804f777e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCPk7g\"}"}